{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `Y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: vectorized the elementwise/indexed sampling statements so that all parameter priors and the protected observation use plain top-level identifiers exactly once. Specifically, `tau[j] ~ gamma(...)` was rewritten as `tau ~ gamma(...)`, the per-`k` prior on `theta[k]` was rewritten as a single top-level `theta ~ normal(mu_theta, sigma_theta)` using deterministic local arrays, and the per-`k` likelihood `Y[k] ~ normal(...)` was rewritten as a single `Y ~ normal(m, sigma_C)` after constructing the same deterministic mean array. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"// Orange Trees 
// http://www.openbugs.net/Examples/Otrees.html

// status: error thrown out during execution immediately 

data {
  int<lower=0> K;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int x;
  array[K, N] real Y;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> tau_C;
  array[K, 3] real theta;
  array[3] real mu;
  array[3] real<lower=0> tau;
}
transformed parameters {
  array[K, 3] real phi;
  array[3] real sigma;
  real sigma_C;
  for (k in 1 : K) {
    phi[k, 1] = exp(theta[k, 1]);
    phi[k, 2] = exp(theta[k, 2]) - 1;
    phi[k, 3] = -exp(theta[k, 3]);
  }
  for (j in 1 : 3) {
    sigma[j] = 1 / sqrt(tau[j]);
  }
  sigma_C = 1 / sqrt(tau_C);
}
model {
  array[K, 3] real mu_theta;
  array[K, 3] real sigma_theta;
  array[K, N] real m;

  tau_C ~ gamma(0.001, 0.001);
  mu ~ normal(0, 100);
  tau ~ gamma(.001, .001);

  for (k in 1 : K) {
    for (j in 1 : 3) {
      mu_theta[k, j] = mu[j];
      sigma_theta[k, j] = sigma[j];
    }
  }
  theta ~ normal(mu_theta, sigma_theta);

  for (k in 1 : K) {
    for (n in 1 : N) {
      m[k, n] = phi[k, 1] / (1 + phi[k, 2] * exp(phi[k, 3] * x[n]));
    }
  }
  Y ~ normal(m, sigma_C);
}
